  "presentation_summary": [
    "20-year-old man initially presented with dysuria and burning micturition; history was notable for allergic asthma and recurrent furuncles with negative HIV serology.",
    "Early workup showed leukocyturia without bacteriuria, later WBC 25.06 x 10^9/L, CRP 109 mg/L, full bladder on ultrasound, and persistent urinary symptoms despite oral ofloxacin.",
    "He returned with abdominal and pelvic pain; prostate ultrasound showed two abscesses and transrectal aspiration yielded purulent fluid.",
    "Six days later he deteriorated with hyperthermia, chills, hypotension, WBC 43 x 10^9/L, lactate 2.90 mmol/L, and MRI evidence of persistent perirectal/prostatic abscesses.",
    "ICU admission CT showed prostatic hypertrophy with several abscesses measuring up to 64 x 21 x 26 mm, perianal infiltration, and enlarged pelvic/retroperitoneal nodes."
  ],
